IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `an72-nouns`
IMPORT `an72-cross-references`

-- Row il-72. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the two items: the provisions each citation names, the status of each provision as the instruments read give it, the repealed provisions, both limbs and how each was read, the flags, the dates, the footnotes, the Law's own commencement, and the page facts of the Interpretation Law.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The assertions that the citations do NOT name a repealed provision are in an72-tests-red.l4.
-- The expected values are hand-written from NOTES.md section 6 (the answer tables), not copied from the references module.

§ `Tests of the readings`

-- The sections each citation names, by number, and the ones a listed instruction repeals.
#ASSERT `the section numbers of the listed provisions` (`the provisions the citing words name` `item I1: section 27(c) names sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)`) EQUALS LIST 2, 3, 4
#ASSERT `the section numbers of the listed provisions` (`the provisions the citing words name that a listed instruction repeals` `item I1: section 27(c) names sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)` `the instructions deposited here`) EQUALS LIST 4
#ASSERT `the section numbers of the listed provisions` (`the provisions the citing words name` `item I2: section 27(a) names section 10 (1) of the Labour Department Ordinance, 1943`) EQUALS LIST 10
#ASSERT `the section numbers of the listed provisions` (`the provisions the citing words name that a listed instruction repeals` `item I2: section 27(a) names section 10 (1) of the Labour Department Ordinance, 1943` `the instructions deposited here`) EQUALS LIST 10
#ASSERT count (`the provisions the citing words name that a listed instruction repeals` `item I1: section 27(c) names sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)` `the instructions deposited here`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`the provisions the citing words name that a listed instruction repeals` `item I2: section 27(a) names section 10 (1) of the Labour Department Ordinance, 1943` `the instructions deposited here`) EQUALS 1

-- The matching rule: a repeal of the whole of section 10 reaches a citation of 10 (1); the repeals of 4 (2) and 5 (d) reach only those subsections.
#ASSERT `the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Labour Department section 10` `Labour Department section 10 (1)`
#ASSERT `the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Labour Department section 4 (2)` `Labour Department section 4 (2)`
#ASSERT `the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Evidence section 4` `Evidence section 4`

-- The status of each provision the citing words name, as the instruments read give it.
#ASSERT `the status of the cited provision` `Evidence section 4` `the instructions deposited here` EQUALS `Repealed by an instrument deposited here`
#ASSERT `the status of the cited provision` `Evidence section 2` `the instructions deposited here` EQUALS NotChecked
#ASSERT `the status of the cited provision` `Evidence section 3` `the instructions deposited here` EQUALS NotChecked
#ASSERT `the status of the cited provision` `Labour Department section 10 (1)` `the instructions deposited here` EQUALS `Repealed by an instrument deposited here`

-- The words each pointer carries, in Latin letters, and how it names the Ordinance.
#ASSERT `pointer in section 27(c): section 2`'s `the words that name the sections, in Latin letters` EQUALS "2"
#ASSERT `pointer in section 27(c): sections 3 and 4`'s `the words that name the sections, in Latin letters` EQUALS "3 and-4"
#ASSERT `pointer in section 27(a): section 10 (1)`'s `the words that name the sections, in Latin letters` EQUALS "10 (1)"
#ASSERT `pointer in section 27(c): section 2`'s `the pointer names the Ordinance` EQUALS `by its title`
#ASSERT `pointer in section 27(c): sections 3 and 4`'s `the pointer names the Ordinance` EQUALS `as the same Ordinance as the pointer before it`
#ASSERT `pointer in section 27(a): section 10 (1)`'s `the pointer names the Ordinance` EQUALS `by its title`

-- The words each repealing instruction carries, item by item, and the number of provisions it repeals.
#ASSERT `SH 444 section 12 repeals`'s `the words that name the repealed sections, item by item, in Latin letters` EQUALS LIST "56", "4"
#ASSERT `SH 164 section 41 repeals`'s `the words that name the repealed sections, item by item, in Latin letters` EQUALS LIST "4 (2), 5 (d) and-10", "39 and-40"
#ASSERT count (`SH 444 section 12 repeals`'s `the provisions it repeals`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT count (`SH 164 section 41 repeals`'s `the provisions it repeals`) EQUALS 5

-- The issue dates the footers print, and the commencement, which no page deposited prints.
#ASSERT `SH 444 section 12 repeals`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 21 1 1965
#ASSERT `SH 164 section 41 repeals`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 3 9 1954
#ASSERT `SH 444 section 12 repeals`'s `the commencement its pages print` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `SH 164 section 41 repeals`'s `the commencement its pages print` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the issue date of SH 81` EQUALS Date 11 7 1951
#ASSERT `the issue date the Gazette supplement prints` EQUALS Date 15 2 1943

-- The Law's own commencement, as its section 39 prints it.
#ASSERT `the commencement of the Law as its section 39 prints it` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 10 1951)

-- Both limbs hold for the two items, and how each was read.
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I1: section 27(c) names sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)`
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I2: section 27(a) names section 10 (1) of the Labour Department Ordinance, 1943`
#ASSERT `item I1: section 27(c) names sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page images, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 27(a) names section 10 (1) of the Labour Department Ordinance, 1943`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page images`
#ASSERT `item I1: section 27(c) names sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `item I2: section 27(a) names section 10 (1) of the Labour Department Ordinance, 1943`'s `limb (b) was read`

-- No instruction in the table of instruments touching the Law names section 27.
#ASSERT NOT (`item I1: section 27(c) names sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)`'s `an instruction in the table of instruments touching the Law names section 27`)
#ASSERT NOT (`item I2: section 27(a) names section 10 (1) of the Labour Department Ordinance, 1943`'s `an instruction in the table of instruments touching the Law names section 27`)

-- The footnotes: the places they name, as typed from the numerals the pages print.
#ASSERT `footnote 2 of SH 81 page 238`'s `the chapter of the Laws of Palestine` EQUALS 34
#ASSERT `footnote 6 of SH 444 page 53`'s `the page of the Laws of Palestine` EQUALS 439
#ASSERT `footnote 5 of SH 444 page 53`'s `the chapter of the Laws of Palestine` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `footnote 1 of SH 81 page 238`'s `the page of the Gazette supplement` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `footnote 1 of SH 164 page 208`'s `the page of the Gazette supplement` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the supplement page that prints section 10 with a subsection (1)` EQUALS 3

-- The two numbers of subsection (a): the page prints 10 (1) and the consolidation prints 4(1); no other word differs.
#ASSERT `the section number the page prints in subsection (a)` EQUALS `pointer in section 27(a): section 10 (1)`'s `the words that name the sections, in Latin letters`
#ASSERT `the section number the consolidation prints in subsection (a)` EQUALS "4(1)"
#ASSERT NOT (`the section number the page prints in subsection (a)` EQUALS `the section number the consolidation prints in subsection (a)`)

-- The Interpretation Law: what the pages print, as page facts. Nothing here says whether section 25 reaches either citation.
#ASSERT `Interpretation Law section 25 as printed`'s `the printed page of the section` EQUALS 305
#ASSERT `Interpretation Law section 1 as printed`'s `the printed page of the section` EQUALS 302
#ASSERT `Interpretation Law section 25 as printed`'s `the issue of Sefer HaChukim` EQUALS 1030
#ASSERT `Interpretation Law section 25 as printed`'s `the issue date the footer of the section prints` EQUALS Date 15 6 1981
#ASSERT `the commencement of the Interpretation Law as its section 32 prints it` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 10 1981)
#ASSERT NOT (`the later instrument names section 25` `SH 1305 touches the Interpretation Law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the later instrument names section 25` `SH 1335 touches the Interpretation Law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the later instrument names section 25` `SH 1481 touches the Interpretation Law`)
#ASSERT `SH 1481 touches the Interpretation Law`'s `the sections of the Interpretation Law it names` EQUALS LIST 1, 3, 22
#ASSERT count `the later instruments that touch the Interpretation Law` EQUALS 3
